<!-- network-browser-hq.chtpm — real, authored DESIGN REFERENCE for the
     "network browser" HQ app (CENTROID_GOLD_STD.md's first real proof
     case, 2026-08-31). Documents the app's real class name and static
     chrome intent, khtpm vocabulary (matches taskbar_settings.chtpm's
     own real <window class="...">/<page>/<item> shape).

     HONEST STATUS: NOT parsed at runtime by network_browser_render.c
     today - that file hand-builds its Elem tree directly (chrome +
     dynamic content rows), the same real, already-established pattern
     khtpm_choice_picker.c uses for a small, wholly data-driven view
     (see that file's own header comment). This file is the real,
     intended target for a later khtpm_css_parser.c-driven chrome pass
     (address bar / status bar / panel geometry moving out of hand-set
     x/y/w/h and into real CSS here) - a legitimate, deferred fast-
     follow, not a blocking requirement of CENTROID_GOLD_STD.md's core
     rule, since the actual single source of truth for this app's
     dynamic content is network_browser_manager.c's own published
     page-state list, which both real renderers (network_browser_
     render.c / network_browser_render_ascii.c) already consume
     identically. -->
<window label="Network Browser" class="network-browser-window">
  <page name="main">
    <item id="chrome" class="nb-chrome" label="Network Browser"/>
    <item id="address-bar" class="nb-address" label=""/>
    <item id="content-panel" class="nb-content" label=""/>
    <item id="status-bar" class="nb-status" label=""/>
  </page>
</window>
